# a gate has failed when it exits non-zero or prints one of these markers
FAIL_RE = re.compile(r"GATE: FAIL|Traceback")        # NOT words like ACCEPTED/FAILED: healthy gate output contains them ("ACCEPTED 0"); the exit status is the real signal

# mutants that no gate can distinguish from the original BY CONSTRUCTION (equivalent mutants); each needs a reason
KNOWN_EQUIVALENT = {
    'M113 irrelevance has no nesting bound': "the bound is a resource guard against pathological input (inference calls the unifier calls inference ..); every well-typed comparison terminates without reaching it, so no test input can distinguish the two",
    'P4 a bad checked function stays callable: its cached value is not dropped on rollback': "eval consults GlobalDef::cached_value only while the global HAS a value (`if (def.value && !no_delta_flag())`); after a rollback it has none, so a stale cache is unreachable, and install_body (mutant P5) drops every cache before a value can appear again. The invalidation in uninstall_body only frees the cached Value early. s20 (C4) pins the observable behaviour: a refused function does not unfold",
    'P5 installing a function body does not drop cached values': "since the reservation rule (mutants R1-R15, gate s20) nothing can mention a function before it is finished, so no cached value anywhere can depend on the function having had no body; the function's own cache is empty until it has a value. Dropping the caches on install is kept as defence in depth (it costs O(#globals) per finished function)",
    'E4 infer(App): after a hidden Pi is exposed the consumed arguments are substituted again': "the exposed Pi is quoted at the current level, so it is closed apart from its own binder: the substitution list then only grows by entries beyond the loose range of every term it is applied to, and instantiate ignores them. The result is the same type, computed with a longer list",
    'E10 check_lambda: the binders opened so far stay recorded after a hidden Pi is exposed': "the same as E4: the quoted Pi mentions the binders opened so far by their context LEVELS, not by loose indices, so the stale entries of the substitution list are beyond the loose range of every term they are applied to",
    'E11 check_lambda: the domain of the expected Pi is not instantiated': "unify evaluates both domains in the context opened so far, whose last entries are exactly the binders of the lambda: a loose index in the uninstantiated domain denotes the same variable as its instantiation. The instantiation only makes equal domains the identical node (so that the shortcut applies and the sort check is skipped); the verdict is the same",
    'E13 check_lambda: a hidden Pi is exposed without substituting the binders opened so far': "the hidden Pi is exposed by EVALUATING the rest of the expected type in the context opened so far, whose last entries are exactly the binders of the lambda, so a loose index in the uninstantiated type denotes the same variable as its instantiation: the value, and everything computed from it, is the same",
    'K17 independent checker: irrelevance gives up at its nesting bound without reporting it': "the flag only changes the TEXT of a refusal, and the bound (4 nested irrelevance inferences) is a resource guard that no well-typed comparison reaches (the same reason as M113)",
    'F5 apply with simp: no ordinary attempt at the end': "the attempt before it is this unification again with only the way a FOUND SOLUTION IS QUOTED changed (folded or fully reduced), and a stored solution is only ever evaluated again, never compared as syntax; no input is known on which the two differ in success (K2 builds the cases where they differ in what is shown). The last attempt stays as the rule that apply with simp refuses nothing the plain apply accepts, and as the one whose error is reported",
    'F20 apply: the conclusion for the ordinary attempts is the folded one': "those attempts unify by EVALUATING the conclusion with every definition unfolded, and evaluating the folded conclusion gives the very value `full` that the quotation was made from: both start from the same value (up to the environments captured inside stuck matches, which unification compares by conversion)",
    'F24 expose_pi_folded drops the arguments a definition takes beyond its lambdas': "a definition applied to more arguments than it has lambdas, whose body is not already a function type, is an ill-typed application, and everything this reads (a goal, the type of a global or of a hypothesis) has been type-checked; when the body is a constant or an application the next round unfolds it to a lambda or to something that is not a Pi and answers nullopt either way",
    'D25 the guarded scope does not restore the compute flag when it ends': "the compute flag is only ever read together with the unfold flag (`guarded_unfold_flag() && guarded_compute_flag()`), and every scope sets both when it begins: a stale compute flag outside every scope is never read, and no scope is opened inside another (apply's attempts, simp_normalize and the display of fields each open one on their own)",
    'D28 guarded unfolding does not check that the decreasing argument is one of the lambdas of the function': "every recursive function is installed through recursive_function_problem, which refuses a decreasing argument that is not one of the lambdas of the body (gate s19: `finish_recursive_function: decreasing argument out of range`), so `d < arity` holds for every function that has recursive_info; the test in apply repeats that condition where the spine is indexed",
    'M12 apply skips drain_pending': "after a successful unify() at the tactic level no deferred constraint is ever pending (every argument meta is applied to the whole context, so its unification is a pattern); drain_pending is exercised by the unifier gate (S3), not by apply",
    'U5 unfold_head_folded unfolds a constructor': "a constructor is declared WITHOUT a value (`GlobalEnv::declare_ctor` passes nullopt), so the test `!def.value` has already returned for it: the removed conjunct `def.ctor_info` is redundant (it documents the intent)",
    'LA14 linarith search: the pruning also looks at the constant row': "the mutant only changes the counts kept for the constant row (`pos`/`neg` under the key `crow`); the test for a dead column skips that row (`if r != crow`), so those counts are never read and the set of surviving columns is the same",
    'LC16 _cancel_order: a lemma with fewer than three leading binders is accepted': "`Proof._peel` stops at the first type that is not a Pi, so when it returns fewer than three holes its body is not a Pi either, and the next check (`pi_parts(body)` is None) raises the very same error with the very same text; the removed test only decides which of two identical refusals is reported",
    'MS4 motive_result_syntactic: a body without loose variables is instantiated all the same': "`instantiate` returns its argument unchanged when the term has no loose bound variable (`vals.empty() || loose_range(t) <= offset`), so the early return only saves building the vector of substituted values",
    'MS8 infer(Match): the type of a match with a motive that is not a lambda is not evaluated': "the type of a match is only ever compared (unify / conv evaluate both sides) or taken apart by infer(App), which unfolds definitions at the head on syntax and evaluates if that does not expose a Pi (`expose_pi_folded`, then `eval`): the evaluated and quoted form is never needed, only something convertible with it, and the application of the motive is that",
    'MS15 scrutinee_family: the type is evaluated once more before its arguments are read': "`cur` is the scrutinee's type after zero or more delta steps of definitions on syntax, so it evaluates to the same value as the type itself (delta and beta are confluent here) and the arguments quoted from the neutral are the same terms",
    'Z19 ring Z: exponents are multiplied where they should be added': "`eadd` only builds the left side that is recorded beside the proof `refl (numeral)` of an exponent equation; the lemma that receives that proof (`pow_split`, `mono_eq`) states the sum itself, over N, and the recorded left side is never read (only the `.proof` of the equation is), so the builder cannot change any proof term -- and the kernel checks the numeral on the right, which the mutants H12/Z18 do change",
}
